{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlkeyaccidental\/value"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"value","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLKeyAccidentalV5valueAA18MXLAccidentalValueOvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental\/value"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLKeyAccidental":{"title":"MXLKeyAccidental","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLKeyAccidental"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlkeyaccidental","abstract":[{"text":"The key-accidental type indicates the accidental to be displayed in a non-traditional key signature,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"represented in the same manner as the accidental type without the formatting attributes.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLKeyAccidental"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLKeyAccidental/value":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlkeyaccidental\/value","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLKeyAccidental\/value","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"title":"value","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same MusicXML semantics."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLAccidentalValue","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","role":"symbol"}}}